# Format:  <proper@email> <commit@email>
#
# BOTH addresses must be inside angle brackets. Verified against git 2.53
# with `git check-mailmap` -- three of the forms the git docs appear to
# allow are silently ignored, so this file is the combination that was
# actually observed to rewrite an identity, not the one that looked right:
#
#   <proper@e> <commit@e>                      MATCHES
#   <proper@e> commit@e                         ignored
#   Proper <proper@e> commit@e                 ignored
#   Proper <proper@e> CommitName <commit@e>     matches, but needs the
#                                               commit's exact display name
#
# Names are preserved; only the address is redirected.

# Claude Code appended this trailer to 22 commits. It resolves to a real
# GitHub account, so the repo grew a second contributor who wrote nothing,
# holds no key and opened no pull request.
<vaskes@kuduza.com> <noreply@anthropic.com>

# 231 commits were recorded against kuduza.ai, a domain that does not exist.
# Unroutable, and matching no account, so none of that work attributes
# anywhere. KuduzaAiLab owns kuduza.com.
<vaskes@kuduza.com> <mavis@kuduza.ai>
<vaskes@kuduza.com> <mavis-agent@kuduza.ai>
<vaskes@kuduza.com> <llamabot@kuduza.ai>
<vaskes@kuduza.com> <mavis@kuduza.com>
<vaskes@kuduza.com> <admin@kuduza.com>

# Deliberately NOT mapped: vaskes@mail.ru, 36 commits. A personal address in
# a public repository. Whether it stays is the owner's call, not a default.